        "Content": "Please note: Some images used in this listing are projected or digitally dressed images. These have been included to help illustrate the potential layout, scale, and possible use of the rooms. They are for visual guidance only and should not be taken as an exact representation of the current furnishings or finishes.\r\n\r\nSpecial Features\r\n•\tDetached traditional two/three-bedroom country residence on approx 1.5 acres, peaceful rural setting in the Ballacolla/Cullahill area\r\n•\tHouse extending to approximately 713 sq. ft. with further potential to extend, accommodation arranged entirely at ground-floor level\r\n•\tGenerous kitchen/dining room approximately 15'10\" x 9'8\"\r\n•\tTwo interconnected living areas offering flexible use\r\n•\tTwo bedrooms and wet-room-style bathroom, \r\n•       Extensive gravelled parking and turning areas, complemented by a private large open garden/grounds extending to over an acre a \r\n         of land offering scope for further landscaping, recreation, or potential future developments.\r\n•\tExtensive gravelled parking and turning areas, large open garden/grounds with scope for further landscaping\r\n•\tHigh ceilings adding character and a greater sense of space\r\n•\tImmediately turnkey with excellent potential for modernisation\r\n•\tMature boundary hedging providing shelter and privacy, gated entrance to private setting\r\n•\tTwo Exceptional detached double garages/workshop accommodation, approximately 1,036 sq. ft. \r\n•\tParticularly attractive proposition for buyers seeking a country property with substantial ancillary space\r\n\r\nSet in a peaceful rural setting in the Ballacolla/Cullahill area of County Laois, Gurteen is a traditional detached two/three bedroom cottage-style residence offering a particularly attractive combination of comfortable accommodation, extensive outside space and substantial double garage/workshop facilities. Gurteen is close to the M8 motorway access.\r\nThere is an appealing simplicity to this property. The house itself is compact and manageable, while the grounds and outbuildings provide considerably more scope than might initially be expected. For purchasers looking for a country home with excellent storage, workshop space or room to pursue a hobby or small enterprise, Gurteen is certainly worthy of consideration.\r\nApproached through a gated entrance, the property enjoys a private setting with mature hedging defining much of the boundary. A large gravelled area surrounds the house and provides excellent parking, turning and set-down space. To the rear is an extensive open garden area which offers considerable potential for landscaping, recreation or simply enjoying the space and privacy of a rural home.\r\nThe detached residence extends to approximately 713 sq. ft. and is laid out entirely at ground-floor level.\r\nThe principal living accommodation has its traditional cottage feel, with high ceilings adding a surprising sense of volume and character. The main living area is arranged around the fireplace and connects through to an additional sitting/living space, creating flexibility in how the rooms are used. This could work particularly well as separate sitting and dining areas, a home office, reading room or bedroom\r\nThe kitchen measures approximately 15'10\" x 9'8\" and is a generous room for a house of this size. There is ample space for dining, together with fitted storage, worktop space and a large window providing plenty of natural light.\r\nThere are two bedrooms. One is an especially long room measuring approximately 7'4\" x 18'5\", while the second measures approximately 9'10\" x 6'11\". The layout provides an opportunity for a new owner to reconsider the internal configuration should they wish to modernise the property and make more efficient use of the available accommodation.\r\nThe bathroom is finished as a practical wet-room-style space with shower, WC and wash-hand basin.\r\nOne of the standout features of Gurteen is undoubtedly the substantial detached garage/workshop accommodation.\r\nThe accompanying floor plan indicates approximately 1,036 sq. ft. of garage space, divided into two sizeable areas measuring approximately 28'2\" x 23'4\" and 15'7\" x 23'10\". This is an enormous advantage and greatly broadens the appeal of the property. Combined with the extensive gravelled yard, there is excellent space for vehicle parking and manoeuvring.\r\nWhether viewed as a permanent home, country retreat, downsizing opportunity or a base for someone requiring serious workshop and storage facilities, Gurteen, Ballacolla, Cullahill, Co. Laois represents an interesting and versatile rural property with plenty of scope for its next owner.\r\n\r\n\r\nThese particulars are issued strictly on the understanding that they do not form part of any contract and are provided, without liability, as a general guide only to what is being offered subject to contract and availability. They are not to be constructed as containing any representation of fact upon which any interested party is entitled to rely. Any intending purchaser or lessee should satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the accuracy of these particulars. The vendor or lessor do not make, give or imply nor is Fran Grincell or its staff authorized to make, give or imply any representation or warranty whatsoever in respect of this property. No responsibility can be accepted for any expenses incurred by intending purchasers in inspecting properties which have been sold, let or withdrawn.\r\n\r\nTHINKING OF SELLING EMAIL OR CALL FOR SALES ADVICE"
